  "numerics, not proof. Jackknife errors use 20 contiguous Monte Carlo blocks; autocorrelation may be understated. n is the number of configurations per run, and each block holds n/20, so at N=8 each block holds 12.",
  "Slice runs at N=6, beta_std=4 used n=600, not the n=1000 of the 4D run at the same coupling.",
  "Slice second differences are forced nonnegative by TwistedLimit.static_upper, so slice runs check the code and test nothing. They are dominated by K(0).",
  "Failure of reflection positivity for 4D-flowed observables of the actual law is numerics only. T=L throughout, and flux wrapping is not separated.",
  "chain entries record the threshold of the first version of the free-chain theorem, for the minor at times 0,1, and the scanned sign change.",
  "polyakov entries: r is half the trace of the winding loop in direction 3. E[r]=0 is exact (TwistedLimit.polyWord_odd), so sample_mean_r nonzero means the run stayed in the cold-start flip sector and does not estimate the mean; G_time is flip-even. neutral_connected_time is the connected function of r^2. Small runs, contiguous blocks, no tunneling test."
